    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d483-a2">

                <pb facs="0579" n="495" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg495"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Lord Lansdowne to Mr.
                            Choate.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-03-28"><hi rendition="#italic">March 28,
                        1903</hi>.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge
                    the receipt of your excellency’s note of the 19th instant, inclosing copies of
                    the President’s proclamation of the convention between the United States and
                    Great Britain for the settlement of questions with respect to the boundary line
                    between Alaska and the British possessions in North America, signed at
                    Washington on the 24th of January last.</p>
                <p>Your excellency at the same time informed me that the President has appointed the
                    Hon. Elihu Root, Secretary of State for War, the Hon. Henry Cabot Lodge, and the
                    Hon. George Turner as American members of the tribunal provided for in the
                    convention.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansdowne.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
